{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Downward Bias: The model consistently underestimates the price level, failing to capture the structural upward shift from ~78 to ~88-91 observed in the true outcomes. Apply a positive level adjustment of +8 to +10 EUR to all forecast horizons.",
    "Lag in Spike Detection: The model exhibits a significant lag in reacting to upward momentum, predicting a slow, linear drift while the true market experiences a sharp, step-like increase. Incorporate a momentum factor that accelerates forecasts when recent history shows consecutive daily gains exceeding 1.5%.",
    "Failure to Capture Volatility Regime: The model assumes mean reversion to the historical average (~78) despite the market entering a higher volatility, higher-mean regime. Override mean-reversion logic when the 18-day history includes values above 80, forcing the forecast to track the new higher baseline.",
    "Sentiment Ignorance: The model ignores the sentiment history (which contains a single positive signal at the start of the period) and treats all days as neutral. Weight the forecast upward when positive sentiment is present in the recent history, even if the immediate price action is flat.",
    "Horizon-Specific Error: The error magnitude increases with the forecast horizon, suggesting the model's long-term drift assumption is too conservative. Apply a convexity correction that increases the slope of the forecast curve as the horizon extends beyond 10 days."
  ]
}
